; Template only — copy to userlist.txt (gitignored, never commit real
; credentials) in this same directory and replace with a REAL md5 hash
; before running docker-compose.prod.yml. Format per line:
;   "username" "md5<32-hex-chars>"
;
; The safest way to get a correct hash is to ask Postgres for the one it
; already computed, rather than hand-computing it yourself — Postgres
; stores exactly this format for md5-authenticated roles:
;
;   psql -h localhost -p 5432 -U whynotgrace -d postgres \
;       -c "SELECT usename, passwd FROM pg_shadow WHERE usename = 'whynotgrace';"
;
; Copy the passwd column's value (it already starts with "md5") verbatim
; into the second field below.
;
; If you'd rather compute it by hand instead (equivalent result):
;   python3 -c "import hashlib,sys; u,p=sys.argv[1],sys.argv[2]; print('md5'+hashlib.md5((p+u).encode()).hexdigest())" whynotgrace 'your-real-password'
;
; Must match POSTGRES_USER/POSTGRES_PASSWORD used by the `backend` and
; `postgres` services in docker-compose.yml / your .env.
"whynotgrace" "md5REPLACE_WITH_REAL_HASH_FROM_PG_SHADOW"
